# SQL Rules

### The complete set
You can think of the rules like this:
Rule	Parent deleted	Child row
CASCADE	Yes	Deleted
RESTRICT	No	Delete blocked
NO ACTION	No	Constraint violation/block
SET NULL	Yes	FK becomes NULL
SET DEFAULT	Yes	FK becomes default
No rule specified	Usually no	Delete blocked
ON UPDATE CASCADE	Parent key changes	Child FK changes too

### CASCADE vs SET NULL vs RESTRICT
This is the most important distinction to understand:
                 Parent deleted
                       │
          ┌────────────┼────────────┐
          ↓            ↓            ↓
       CASCADE       SET NULL     RESTRICT
          │            │            │
          ↓            ↓            ↓
   Delete child    Keep child    Keep child
                  FK = NULL     Delete blocked
